{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reciprocal reciprocal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md","fileName":"Reciprocal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reciprocal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Fractions and Decimal Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Identity Element","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reciprocal reciprocal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md","fileName":"Reciprocal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reciprocal","heading":"Reciprocal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The reciprocal of a nonzero number is the value that multiplies with it to produce the multiplicative [[Identity Element]] one. For a nonzero fraction,\n\n$$\\left(\\frac{c}{d}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{d}{c}.$$\n\nThus the reciprocal of (3/5) is (5/3). Division by a nonzero fraction is multiplication by its reciprocal:\n\n$$\\frac{a}{b}\\div\\frac{c}{d}=\\frac{a}{b}\\cdot\\frac{d}{c}.$$\n\nZero has no reciprocal because no number multiplied by zero equals one.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Identity Element","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reciprocal reciprocal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reciprocal.md","fileName":"Reciprocal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reciprocal","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Identity Element","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}